Description: avcodec/ac3_parser: separate sync headers from full bitstream info
 The sync scanner only buffers seven bytes. Since 117343c0ba expanded
 ff_ac3_parse_header() to parse all bitstream information, it also reads
 uninitialized bytes beyond that prefix. A random dependent-channel map
 can reject a valid sync word and corrupt packet boundaries. This causes
 intermittent eac3-5 and eac3-core-bsf FATE failures, even with one
 thread.
 .
 Restore the bounded header reader and put metadata parsing in a full
 header helper. Keep the existing full-header callers on that helper and
 preserve the sync scanner's substream-ID restriction. Account for all 56
 prefix bits, including both mix-level fields in AC-3 3/2 mode.
 .
 Valgrind reports uninitialized reads on master and none with this
 change.
 .
